   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "the:regret",
    "number": "Theorem 6.1",
    "quote": "When $\\Xc$ is finite, set the confidence intervals ... with $\\betat(\\delta) = C_k+\\frac{\\sigma}{\\lambda}\\sqrt{2\\log(\\frac{4R|\\Xc|}{\\delta})}$. Under Assumptions~\\ref{ass:f_norm},~\\ref{ass:noise},~\\ref{ass:sub-exp}, with probability at least $1-\\delta$, the regret of BPE-Delay is bounded by $\\Rc(T) = \\Oc\\left(\\betat(\\delta)\\log\\log(T)\\sqrt{T\\Gamma_k(T)} + \\E[\\tau]\\right)$."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "gamma_T is the maximum information gain Gamma_k(T). Regret defined through f values (no noise) but bound holds w.p. 1-delta. Proof actually gives C_k E[tau] term."
  },
